# Maewyn Ashvale - druid of the deep hills (Act 1 sidequest). Sends the guild
# message; recruitable companion.
# VOICE: terse. A woman of few words who keeps her thoughts to herself. Her
# lines run short; the narration, the raven, and her pauses do the talking.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Maewyn

entry joined if in_party()
entry sent if flag(TSC_MaewynSent)

== start ==
The cottage door opens before you knock. The woman in it has grey-green eyes, a raven on her shoulder, and the expression of someone who knew you were coming but is still unimpressed.

She looks at your boots. At your sword. At the guild's ink stains on your cuff. The raven clicks its beak.

"Business, rider. Mind the beds."

* "Serra Voss's company needs a message carried to the Wayfarers' Guild." -> message
* "Your bees are wintering early. That's a hard-cold sign, this far from frost." -> bees
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynBees)
    check Nature 7 -> bees | bees_miss
* "How did you know I was coming?" -> hills

== bees ==
Maewyn stops. Actually stops, hand on the doorframe, and looks at you properly for the first time.

"...They are. Six weeks early." A long pause, in which something is decided. She steps back from the door.

"Come in. Wipe your boots."

* "The business is a message for the guild." -> message
    do flag(TSC_MaewynBees); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)

== bees_miss ==
Maewyn follows your gesture to the hives. Snorts.

"Sulking, not wintering. I moved their south board Tuesday."

That appears to be the whole conversation.

* "Then I'll get to my business: a message for the guild." -> message

== hills ==
"The hills talk. I listen."

She studies you a moment, then steps back from the door, which you suspect is as close to an invitation as she gives.

"You're the rider they've been muttering about. Out with it."

* "A message to the guild. They lost their raven." -> message

== message ==
"Lost their raven." The one on her shoulder clicks its beak, and Maewyn's mouth twitches; on anyone else it would be a smile.

She considers you for a long, unhurried moment. You get the sense of a great deal being thought and none of it being said.

"Not for the guild. For Serra. Debts matter."

She holds out a hand for the letter.

* "Here. The guild will know the party lives." -> agreed
* [Insight] "This grove is lonely, Maewyn. Even with the ravens." -> lonely
    if passive(Insight, 8)

== agreed ==
Maewyn signals a nearby raven, ties the message with a strip of bark-cord, murmurs something to the raven that is definitely not any language you know, and casts it into the sky.

"Inside a week."

She watches the bird shrink to a speck. Just when you decide she has finished with you:

"The ettersnap. When it speaks - listen to what it doesn't say."

* "How did you know about the ettersnap?" -> ettersnap
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)
* "Come with me. We could use your help." -> recruit
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)
* "Thank you, Maewyn. And the advice is noted." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)

== ettersnap ==

"My birds watch."

Nothing further is offered.

* "Come with me. We could use your help." -> recruit
* "Thank you, Maewyn. I'll leave you to your bees and birds." -> end

== lonely ==
The raven goes very still. So does Maewyn.

"...The hills talk," she says at last, quieter. "They don't answer."

She takes the letter from your hand without ceremony, and does not look at you.

"I'll send it. And I'll think on the other thing."

* "Then ask it plainly I shall: ride with me, Maewyn." -> recruit
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent); affinity(+5)
* "Thank you, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent); affinity(+5)

== recruit ==
Maewyn looks at her grove - the beds, the hives, the mossy quiet - for a long moment. Thirty years of keeping, weighed in silence.

"The hills can hold it a while."

She whistles; the second raven drops from the eaves to her shoulder.

"Try to deserve it."

* "Welcome to the company, Maewyn." -> welcomed
    do join_party(); affinity(+5)
* "Take a day to be sure. I'll return." -> end

== welcomed ==
She pulls the door shut behind her without locking it and falls in beside you.

"Serra's hunt. Tell me. Walking's for talking."

It is the most words you will get out of her at once for some time.

* "This way, Maewyn."

== sent ==
Maewyn is in her garden, unsurprised as ever. She doesn't stop working.

"Message flew. Something else?"

* "The offer stands: ride with me." -> recruit
* "Just passing. Peace on your grove." -> end

== joined ==
Maewyn is watching the horizon the way other people read. She speaks without turning.

"Too quiet here. Don't trust it."

A beat.

"What?"

* "I wouldn't mind learning a thing or two from you." -> druid_teaching
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynTaught)
* "How fares the grove without its keeper?" -> grove_talk
    if affinity(>=10) and not flag(TSC_MaewynGroveTalk)
* "About your cellar, Maewyn..." -> cellar_caught
    if flag(TSC_MaewynCellarTheft) and not flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired)
* "Carry on, Maewyn."

== cellar_caught ==
Maewyn doesn't look at you. Corvus does, unblinking.

"Thirty years, that lock."

She lets the silence do the rest of the accusing. It is very good at it.

"Keep the book. You could have asked."

* "It won't happen again, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired)
* "The company's supplies are the company's business." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired); affinity(-5)

== grove_talk ==
Maewyn is quiet long enough that you think she won't answer.

"The cat has the run of it. The bees will sulk and thrive. Door's not locked - a locked door in the hills is a dare."

Corvus shifts on her shoulder. When she speaks again it is nearly too quiet to catch.

"Thank you for asking. Nobody does."

* "We'll walk you back someday, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynGroveTalk); grant_xp(10)

== druid_teaching ==
She looks at you a moment, then settles onto a stone as if she'd picked it out an hour ago.

"Sit. First lesson is sitting."

That evening, and for several after, she teaches - mostly without words: how to sit until the birds forget you; which silences mean weather and which mean wolves; what the green things say under the soil, and what they'll say to you.

* [Learn the Druid's way] "I hear it now. Faintly." -> end
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynTaught)
    do flag(TSC_MaewynTaught); learn_class(TSC_Class_Druid); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)
* "This is... a lot of sitting, Maewyn." -> end
